From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Describe the S8003 chip in a variant
 table

The A8 (T7000) runs the A9's GFX firmware family on the same META: the
same LDR image format, loader, windows, rings, events, slots and job
records, with different sizes, counts, register choices and a different
parameter manager. Rather than a second chip file that copies the boot,
ring and slot code, give the S8003 chip file a table of what differs.

struct s8003_variant holds the sizes (image, root and shared memory, the
object table, a ring lane's indices), the slots (count, first, how many
a VM takes), where the channels are, whether the firmware needs the
host's cache-line reads, and the steps whose structure differs: image
configuration, mapping, init data, boot, release, stop, idle, doorbell,
the first command, a VM's mappings and PM sets, job preparation and
submission, completion and the hang report. The chip's ops call through
it.

The A9's table holds today's constants and functions unchanged, so the
A9 runs exactly as before: every value the shared code now reads from
the table is the constant it used, and every hook is the function that
ran in its place.

Assisted-by: LLM
